        <!-- KEY CHALLENGES BOX -->
        <mxCell id="challenges-box" value="🎯 KEY TECHNICAL CHALLENGES" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffebee;strokeColor=#c62828;strokeWidth=3;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="800" width="1620" height="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="challenges-list" value="1. **Exactly-once money movement**: Client retries due to timeout → idempotency key prevents double-charge. 2. **ACID guarantees**: Payment + ledger + outbox in ONE transaction (partial writes = money creation/loss). 3. **Race conditions**: Two concurrent debits from same account → optimistic locking prevents overdraft. 4. **Event loss prevention**: App crashes after DB write but before Kafka publish → outbox pattern guarantees delivery. 5. **Bank API failures**: Timeout/network error → saga pattern with compensating transactions (not 2PC). 6. **Immutable audit trail**: Ledger never updated/deleted → regulatory compliance, fraud investigation. 7. **Reconciliation**: Our ledger vs bank statement CSV mismatch → final safety net catches what automation missed. 8. **Cross-shard transactions**: User transfers between accounts on different shards → distributed saga or 2PC within our system only." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=9" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="830" width="1600" height="50" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- Real-World Analogy -->
        <mxCell id="analogy-box" value="🏪 REAL-WORLD ANALOGY" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1f5fe;strokeColor=#01579b;strokeWidth=3;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="910" width="1620" height="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="analogy-text" value="Traditional cash register: Cashier takes money, puts in till, gives receipt. If cashier drops money before reaching till, customer loses. **Payment system automates this with guarantees**: You swipe card (payment initiated, idempotency key = receipt number). System writes to ledger book (MySQL transaction = till record). Bank approves (async, like manager checking safe). Ledger shows two lines: -Rs.100 from your account (DEBIT), +Rs.100 to merchant (CREDIT). These cancel to zero. If manager doesn't respond in 30 sec, we ask again (retry). If register crashes mid-write, outbox relay picks up and finishes. Nightly reconciliation = manager counts safe vs ledger book. The hard part: all this coordination must be bulletproof — no money created, lost, or moved twice, even when network/DB/bank fails mid-operation." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=9" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="940" width="1600" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>